# MFC patterns (Envy)

## UI/threading hard rules
- Never block the UI thread on network/disk operations.
- Never touch UI controls from worker threads. Use `PostMessage` / message handlers.
- Use existing synchronization patterns (`CCriticalSectionPtr`, `CQuickLock`, `CLocked<T>`) for shared state.

## Message maps
- Use `DECLARE_MESSAGE_MAP()` / `BEGIN_MESSAGE_MAP` consistently.
- Handler naming: `On...` (`afx_msg void OnSize(...)`, `afx_msg LRESULT On...(...)`).

## Strings + Unicode
- Prefer `CString` and `_T("...")` for UI/MFC-facing strings.
- Treat all paths/strings as Unicode (UTF-16).

## GUI resource de-duplication (non-negotiable)
Before adding ANY new dialog/control/menu/toolbar/accelerator/icon/string-table entry:
- Search existing resources by **ID**, **symbolic name**, and **caption text**.
- Search code for usage (`IDD_*`, `ID_*`, `GetDlgItem`, `DDX_*`, message map IDs).
- Prefer extending/reusing an existing resource.

If a new resource is unavoidable, you MUST provide (in your output):
- Existing resources checked (IDs/names/text searched)
- Chosen free slot / new ID (and why it won’t collide)
- Where used (file path + class/function)

If you cannot verify existing resources: do NOT create the new resource yet.
